-- NEGATIVE fixture for the rule-date interval table (spec §15.3, R10).
--
-- The `OTHERWISE` is itself a guarded chain. On the ORDINARY path
-- `expandOtherwise` splices such a chain's rows into the table, and reports the
-- rows it declines to splice as `D-FLATTENCAP`. The dated path never calls
-- `flattenGuarded`, so it would have collapsed the whole nested chain into ONE
-- floor-row output entry -- silently, because `datedTable` passes no capped
-- bodies and so no cap note can fire.
--
-- So the nested-chain test counts the `OTHERWISE` as an arm body, and this
-- chain is `NotDated`: the existing path, the existing findings, and the rows
-- the inner chain contributes still present.
--
-- Expected: NO D-DATEDCHAIN (this is not a refusal, it is a decline), a `FIRST`
-- table, and MORE than the two rules a dated table would have emitted.
--
-- NEVER added to `goldenSubjects`. Asserted from jl4/tests/DmnExport.hs.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

§ `nested otherwise under a dated arm`

TIMEZONE IS "Asia/Singapore"

GIVETH A DATE
`the 2024 rate change` MEANS Date 1 1 2024

ASSUME `no GST rate exists before commencement` IS A NUMBER

ASSUME `the transitional relief applies` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVETH A NUMBER
`GST rate percent` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `RULES EFFECTIVE DATE` AT LEAST `the 2024 rate change` THEN 9
           OTHERWISE  IF   `the transitional relief applies`
                      THEN 0
                      ELSE `no GST rate exists before commencement`
